  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing South-South and triangular industrial cooperation through UNIDO Centre for South-South Industrial Cooperation China (Phase 4)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNIDO Centre for South-South Industrial Cooperation (UCSSIC China) was established in July 2008 following the conclusion of a MoU between UNIDO and the Government of China in September 2006 on enhancing South-South industrial cooperation and the signature of a project document entitled #Establishment of a UNIDO Centre for South-South Industrial Cooperation, Beijing, China# in August 2007.  Upon completion of the phase 1 and phase 2 of the project and based on the achievements accomplished by UCSSIC China, the phase 3 of the project, entitled #Supporting the UNIDO Centre for South-South Industrial Cooperation in China (Phase 3)# commenced in 2020 to further enhance South-South industrial cooperation between the host Country China and other developing countries through increased effectiveness of the Centre. During the phase 3 of the project, UCSSIC China actively played its role as a platform for China to promote South-South Cooperation, further strengthened its partnership with other developing countries, promoted the green development of industrial parks, strengthened the knowledge and experience-sharing, and promoted capacity-building and technology transfer between China and other developing countries.  UNIDO has consistently attached great importance to South-South and Triangular Industrial Cooperation (SSTI</narrative>
  </description>
